<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 690 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 690 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 690 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>			    EARLY	1200 GMT   1400 GMT   LATE</p>
<p> FORECAST SHORTAGE    1.2 BLN    1.2 BLN    1.35 BLN   =</p>
<p> CUMULATIVE SUPPLY    =	    600 MLN!   1.29 BLN   =</p>
<p>DETAILS</p>
<p> BAND 1 T-BILLS	 =	    =	     27 MLN*    =</p>
<p> BAND 1 BANK BILLS    =	    =	    663 MLN*    =</p>
<p>* INTEREST RATE 5-15/16 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
<p>! INCLUDES 600 MLN STG REPO EXPIRING FEBRUARY 3 AND 4 AT 5-31/32 PCT (INDICATES UNCHANGED BASE RATES)</p>
</text>
